+// g-lab-bit fork (annot_ap_oc.patch)
+// Experimental API.
+// Put the normal appearance of |annot| under optional content: every object
+// of the appearance gets nested marked content
+//   /OC /<name> BDC ... EMC
+// one level per OCG in |ocg_indices| (indices into /OCProperties /OCGs;
+// ocg_indices[0] is the outermost, e.g. the top ancestor layer; duplicates
+// are ignored). Viewers that honour marked content in appearances (PDFium,
+// pdf.js) then hide the markup when ANY of the groups is off, through
+// /OCProperties /D or FPDFDoc_SetOCGViewState(). Use together with
+// FPDFAnnot_SetOCMembership() for readers that use annotation /OC.
+// PDFKit ignores optional content in annotation appearances.
+//
+// ONLY for appearances built with FPDFAnnot_AppendObject(): the appearance is
+// re-serialised from PDFium's page objects, which can lose content another
+// producer wrote. To rebuild an appearance of an annotation already in the
+// file without modifying its existing stream object, call
+// FPDFAnnot_SetAP(annot, FPDF_ANNOT_APPEARANCEMODE_NORMAL, NULL) on a freshly
+// obtained annotation handle, then FPDFAnnot_AppendObject().
+//
+// The marked appearance is written to a NEW stream object and /AP /N is
+// repointed to it (the previous stream is left untouched and unreferenced),
+// so FPDF_SaveIncrementalObjects() writes it as a new object reachable from
+// the annotation (list the annotation or its /Annots holder). /Properties
+// entries in the new stream's /Resources: an existing entry is reused only if
+// it already refers to the group; new entries are named /RpOC<n> (an unused
+// name); /RpOC<n> entries referring to an OCG that is no longer in the set are
+// removed.
+//   appearance_mode - only FPDF_ANNOT_APPEARANCEMODE_NORMAL is supported.
+//   count           - 0 removes the /OC marks.
+// Existing /OC marks are replaced, other marks are kept (the /OC levels are
+// added inside them). Objects appended later with FPDFAnnot_AppendObject()
+// are not marked: call this again afterwards. Supported for the subtypes
+// FPDFAnnot_AppendObject() supports. Fails, without changing anything, for an
+// invalid index, a direct OCG, an /AP that is not a direct dictionary whose
+// /N refers to a stream, or a stream without direct /Resources.
+// FPDFDoc_DeleteOCG() does not remove these marks: re-mark the annotation
+// before deleting a group it uses.
+FPDF_EXPORT FPDF_BOOL FPDF_CALLCONV
+FPDFAnnot_SetAPOptionalContent(FPDF_DOCUMENT document,
+                               FPDF_ANNOTATION annot,
+                               FPDF_ANNOT_APPEARANCEMODE appearance_mode,
+                               const int* ocg_indices,
+                               int count);
+
 // Experimental API.
 // Get the total number of objects in |annot|, including path objects, text
 // objects, external objects, image objects, and shading objects.
